The site is blank because **`useState`** is not imported in your `App.jsx` file, which causes React to crash immediately when the page loads.

You also have a small typo where you passed `setSideabr` instead of `setSidebar` to the `Navbar` component, which will cause a crash when clicking the menu button.

---

### The Fix

Open **`src/App.jsx`** and replace its contents with the code below:

```javascript
import React, { useState } from 'react' // Fixed: Added { useState }
import Navbar from "./Components/Navbar/Navbar";
import { Routes, Route } from 'react-router-dom'; 
import Home from './Pages/Home/Home';             
import Video from './Pages/Video/Video';            

const App = () => {

  const [sidebar, setSidebar] = useState(true);

  return (
    <div>
      {/* Fixed: changed setSideabr to setSidebar */}
      <Navbar setSidebar={setSidebar} />
      <Routes>
        <Route path="/" element={<Home sidebar={sidebar} />} />
        <Route path='/video/:categoryId/:videoId' element={<Video />} />
      </Routes>
    </div>
  )
}

export default App
```
